From add1d22fd2b506948c994dd34cd454048323317f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Joonhoe Kim <26rote@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 01:33:01 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: configs: baldur: do not set the clock from the PMIC
 RTC

The PMIC RTC on this board counts from 1970; the firmware keeps the
offset to real time to itself. RTC_DRV_PM8XXX is a module, so with
RTC_HCTOSYS the kernel sets the system clock from it when the module
loads, after systemd has advanced the clock to the time it saved. The
clock then runs in 1970 until NTP synchronises it, and files created in
that window, such as /tmp/.X11-unix, look decades old: tmpfiles-clean
removes them 15 minutes after boot, and the next GNOME login fails to
start Xwayland.

Signed-off-by: Joonhoe Kim <26rote@gmail.com>
---
 arch/arm64/configs/baldur.fragment | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/configs/baldur.fragment b/arch/arm64/configs/baldur.fragment
index a5f6fafd0..0ff53c11a 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/configs/baldur.fragment
+++ b/arch/arm64/configs/baldur.fragment
@@ -113,6 +113,8 @@ CONFIG_PINCTRL_SM8650_LPASS_LPI=m
 # ("install snd-pcm ... && modprobe snd-seq"); without it that modprobe fails and
 # the sound card never appears. Modules only.
 CONFIG_SND_SEQUENCER=m
+# The PMIC RTC counts from 1970; the firmware keeps the offset to real time.
+# CONFIG_RTC_HCTOSYS is not set
 # /sys/power/pm_test, pm_print_times, pm_debug_messages -- without these
 # a "pm_test" write silently fails and "echo freeze > state" really suspends.
 CONFIG_PM_DEBUG=y
-- 
2.53.0

